Title: Predicted Means for Linear and Semiparametric Models
Description: Predicted means, standard errors, contrasts, multiple comparisons,
    permutation and bootstrap tests, R-squared and diagnostics for models fitted by
    'aov', 'lm', 'glm', 'gls', 'lme', 'lmer', 'glmer', 'glmmTMB', 'gam' and 'semireg'.
    Defaults are chosen on evidence: Kenward-Roger degrees of freedom and adjusted
    standard errors for REML 'lmer' fits (Kenward and Roger (1997) <doi:10.2307/2533558>),
    permutation p-values (b+1)/(B+1), stratum standard errors for 'aov' models with
    Error() terms as in 'Genstat', and equal-weight means over observed cells with a
    warning. Results are tested against 'SAS' PROC MIXED and 'Genstat' output and
    the 'pbkrtest', 'nlme' and 'emmeans' packages. Functions stop with a message
    rather than return a wrong result, give one-line advice triggered by the data,
    and give the same resampling results for any number of cores.
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0), lme4, nlme
